# Seed lists are NOT tracked in this repository, and must not become tracked.
#
# This repository is public. A seed list is a curated set of coordinates drawn
# from a private source, so its *contents* are sensitive even though nothing in
# it is secret line by line: the set itself discloses which parts of an
# ecosystem an internal project depends on. Redacting a name from the file
# would not fix that -- the list is the disclosure.
#
# They are also genuinely runtime inputs. Changing which roots we explore
# should be a file sync on the host, not an image rebuild plus a coordinated
# cutover (deploy/quadlet/collectors/checkpoint-cutover.md).
#
# Deployment: install to /etc/containers/systemd/seeds/ on the collector host,
# mode 644. pg-collect@.container bind mounts that directory read-only at
# /seeds. See README.md here for the file format and the failure modes.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
